    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d30-a5">

                <pb facs="0081" n="71" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg71"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Steamer Kearsarge,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Off Queenstown,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 7, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inform you that I came
                    to, off Queenstown, for the purpose of landing sixteen refugees who had
                    concealed themselves on board this ship prior to her departure from Queenstown,
                    on the 5th of November. I learn here that an attempt has been made to magnify
                    this circumstance for purposes unfriendly to the United States. I have,
                    therefore, given to the American consul my certificate, with a representation of
                    the circumstances by the executive officer of this ship, and I have directed the
                    consul to hand you a copy of the same.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JNO. A. WINSLOW, <hi rendition="#italic">Captain.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Rear-Admiral Sir <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis T. Jones</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Com’dg H. M. Naval Forces, Coast of
                        Ireland.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
